JSCOnly: select the Unix memory-pressure handler on QNX.

Linking fails with:

    MemoryPressureHandler.cpp: undefined reference to
        WTF::MemoryPressureHandler::holdOffTimerFired()

MemoryPressureHandler.h declares m_holdOffTimer and holdOffTimerFired() for
"OS(LINUX) || OS(FREEBSD) || OS(QNX)", and unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp
defines them -- it already has an OS(QNX) branch that reads the resident set
size with devctl(DCMD_PROC_ASINFO) on /proc/self/ctl.  WTF knows about QNX; the
JSCOnly platform list simply had no QNX case, so the build fell through to
generic/MemoryPressureHandlerGeneric.cpp, which does not define the members the
header declared.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformJSCOnly.cmake
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformJSCOnly.cmake
@@ -116,6 +116,18 @@
 
         unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp
     )
+elseif (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "QNX")
+    # MemoryPressureHandler.h declares m_holdOffTimer and holdOffTimerFired()
+    # under "OS(LINUX) || OS(FREEBSD) || OS(QNX)", and the definition lives in
+    # unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp -- which already carries an OS(QNX)
+    # branch reading rss through devctl(DCMD_PROC_ASINFO) on /proc/self/ctl.
+    # Only this platform list was missing QNX, so the build fell through to the
+    # generic handler and left holdOffTimerFired() undefined at link time.
+    list(APPEND WTF_SOURCES
+        generic/MemoryFootprintGeneric.cpp
+
+        unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp
+    )
 else ()
     list(APPEND WTF_SOURCES
         generic/MemoryFootprintGeneric.cpp
